 "conclusion": "The confound is real: named words are rarer pre-2022 (Spearman -0.57 between log baseline frequency and named status). The DECAY-DEPTH contrast does not survive frequency matching at any floor (matched sign p 0.31 to 0.66, regression coefficient on named +3 +- 30 at the loosest floor where power is greatest). The PEAK-TIMING clustering partly survives: named words peak in the publicity-adjacent window 7 of 10 times against 5 of 22 for unnamed, permutation p 0.015 unstratified and 0.070 stratified on baseline frequency. Word-level decay depth is therefore NOT independent evidence for avoidance. Timing remains, and is marginal on its own."
